{
  "dom_id": "step-q183300",
  "name": "Question 7",
  "problem": "$\\,$ $a<8$ and $a>2.$\n\nThe negation of the composite predicate above is the following:\n\n$\\,$ \n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}{{field-3}}",
  "worked_solution": "De Morgan's law for conjunctions states that\n\n$$\n¬(A∧B)=¬A∨¬B.\n$$\n\nSo, the negation of \"$a<8$ and $a>2$ \" is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬(a<8\\text{ and }a>2) & ≡¬(a<8∧a>2) \\\\  & ≡¬(a<8)∨¬(a>2) \\\\  & ≡a\\ge 8∨a\\le 2 \\\\  & ≡a\\ge 8\\text{ or }a\\le 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
